INSERT INTO `ordinance_files` (`file_id`, `ordinance_id`, `uploaded_by`, `year`, `file_name`, `file_url`, `file_size`, `file_type`, `extracted_text`, `uploaded_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1, 1, 1, NULL, '2022,amending-sp-ordinance,hon-ma-bella-c-javier.pdf', 'ordinances/provincial/2022,amending-sp-ordinance,hon-ma-bella-c-javier.pdf', 1343077, 'application/pdf', 'First District\n       HON. MARIE YVONNE V. PALMA\n                        Assistant Floor Leader \n         Chairman: Senior Citizen, Differently Abled \nPersons,\n         Women, Children, Family & Other Social Services,\n         Education, Science, Arts & Culture\n       HON. ALLAN B. ESCAMILLAN \n          Chairman: Food & Agriculture, Energy, \n          Electrification, Public Utilities & Transportation\n       HON. JESSIE R. LAGAS \n          Chairman: Land Use, Housing, Rural & Urban \n          Development, Ethics & Good Government, and\n          Environment, Forest, Rivers & Inland Waters\n       HON. PEPITO S. YANGA, JR. \n       Chairman: Human Rights, Labor, Justice and\n          Employment, and Privileges, \n       ATTY. MARLO C. BANCORO \n          Chairman: Finance, Revenue, Way & Means, \n          Rules, Ordinances & Resolutions, Infrastructure,\n          Public   Works, & Engineering, Asset & Manage-\n          ment, Franchises, Games, & Amusements,\n          Municipal Affairs, & Legislative Oversight\n                Second District\n      HON. RICHARD D. OLEGARIO\n                              Floor Leader\n         Chairman:   Appropriations, Cooperatives Deve-\n         lopment, NGOs, PO’s, People Empowerment, \n         Gender & Development  & Steering Committee & \n         Inter-Agency Affairs, \nHON. MA. BELLA C. JAVIER \n        Chairman : Health, Information Communication\n        Technology (ICT), Rural Impact Sourcing (RIS) &\n        Computerization, International Relations & External\n        Affairs, & Economic Enterprise and Privatization\nHON. GERALD M. ACOSTA \n                   Assistant Floor Leader\n Chairman : Mining and Other Resources, & \nFishery\n        and Coastal Resources. \nHON. CHENNIE S. DELOS REYES \n        Chairman : Peace  &  Order, Calamities, Fire & \n        Public Safety\n      HON. MARIA ESPERANZA CORAZON D.\nRILLERA-HADJIULA\n       Chairman: Tourism, & Appointments and Other\n       Personnel Concerns\nSectoral Representatives \n       HON. JERRY R. LAGAS \n          President : Liga ng mga Barangay\n          Chairman: Barangay Affairs, Trade , Industry & \n          Special Investments\n  \n      HON. DARA MAY L. CATALUÑA \n         President : Provincial Councilor’s League\n        Chairman: Legislative Tracking & Analysis\n      HON. NATH ANTHONY R. EUDELA\n        President : Sangguniang Kabataan, \n        Chairman: Youth & Sports Development\n      HON. ABDURAUP A. ABISON \n       Representative : Provincial Indigenous People’s\n        Chairman: Muslim, Indigenous Peoples and\n        Cultural Communities\n   \n  \n \n  \n  \n \n  \nRepublic of the Philippines\nPROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY\n                                    Municipality of Ipil\nEXCERPT from the minutes of the 1\nst\n Regular Session of the 8\nth \nSangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga \nSibugay held at the Legislative Building, Capitol Hills, Ipil Heights, \nIpil, Zamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\n  \n    Author: Hon. MA. BELLA C. JAVIER \n      (Board Member, 2\nND\n District)\nAN ORDINANCE AMENDING SP ORDINANCE 2022-595, \nUNDER PARAGRAPH 1, PERSONNEL SCHEDULE BY \nDEPARTMENTS/OFFICE/UNIT BY CHANGING THE \nPOSITION TITLES UNDER THE OFFICE OF THE \nPROVINCIAL GOVERNOR, OFFICE OF THE PROVINCIAL \nVICE-GOVERNOR AND SANGGUNIANG \nPANLALAWIGAN PURSUANT TO CIVIL SERVICE \nCOMMISSION (CSC) MEMORANDUM CIRCULAR NO. \n12, S. 2011. \nBE ENACTED, by the 8\nTH\n SANGGUNIANG PANLALAWIGAN \nof the PROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY , \nin session duly assembled, and\nORDAINED THAT:\nSection 1. Title – This ordinance shall be known and \nthereafter referred to as “AN ORDINANCE AMENDING SP \nORDINANCE 2022-595, UNDER PARAGRAPH 1, PERSONNEL \nSCHEDULE BY DEPARTMENTS/OFFICE/UNIT BY CHANGING \nTHE POSITION TITLES UNDER THE OFFICE OF THE \nPROVINCIAL GOVERNOR, OFFICE OF THE PROVINCIAL VICE-\nGOVERNOR AND SANGGUNIANG PANLALAWIGAN PURSUANT \nTO CIVIL SERVICE COMMISSION (CSC) MEMORANDUM \nCIRCULAR NO. 12, S. 2011”.\nSection 2. BASIS – Civil Service Commission (CSC) \nMemorandum Circular No. 12, S. 2011 dated February 1, 2011, in re: \nRevised Guidelines on the Determination of Positions in the Local \nGovernment as Primarily Confidential, in relation to CSC Resolution \nNo. 1100187, adopts guidelines/policies on the declaration of positions \nin the local government units as primarily confidential. \nSection 3. Changing  of Positions – There is hereby re-titling \nand changing in the plantilla positions of the Province of Zamboanga \nSibugay, pursuant to CSC MC No. 12, s 2011, the following, viz: \n3.1 OFFICE OF THE PROVINCIAL GOVERNOR\nFROM\nITEM \nNO.\nSALARY \nGRADE TO\nITEM \nNO.\nSALARY \nGRADE\n1Senior Administrative \nAssistant III\n5 15\nPrivate Secretary \nI\n5 15\n2Administrative Aide IV8 4 Driver II 8 4\n3Administrative Aide IV9 4 Driver II 9 4\n4Administrative Aide IV10 4 Driver II 10 4\n\nFROM\nITEM \nNO.\nSALARY \nGRADE	TO\nITEM \nNO.\nSALARY \nGRADE\nOFFICE OF THE PROVINCIAL GOVERNOR\n5Administrative Aide III 11 3 Driver I	11 3\n6Administrative Aide III 12 3 Driver I	12 3\n7Administrative Aide III 13 3 Driver I	13 3\n8Administrative Aide III 51 3 Driver I	51 3\n9Administrative Aide III 56 3 Driver I	56 3\n10Administrative Aide III 59 3 Driver I	59 3\n11Administrative Aide III 61 3 Driver I	61 3\n3.2. OFFICE OF THE PROVINCIAL VICE-GOVERNOR\nFROM\nITEM \nNO.\nSALARY \nGRADE	TO\nITEM \nNO.\nSALARY \nGRADE\n1\nSenior Administrative \nAssistant III\n3 15Private Secretary II 3 15\n2\nSenior Administrative \nAssistant III\n4 15Private Secretary II 4 15\n3Administrative Assistant V 5 11Private Secretary I 5 11\n4Administrative Aide IV 10 4 Driver II	10 4\n3.3.  SANGGUNIANG PANLALAWIGAN\nFROM\nITEM \nNO.\nSALARY \nGRADE	TO\nITEM \nNO.\nSALARY \nGRADE\n1Administrative Assistant V 20 11Private Secretary I 20 11\n2Administrative Assistant V 21 11Private Secretary I 21 11\n3Administrative Assistant V 22 11Private Secretary I 22 11\n4Administrative Assistant V 23 11Private Secretary I 23 11\n5Administrative Assistant V 24 11Private Secretary I 24 11\n6Administrative Assistant V 40 11Private Secretary I 40 11\n7Administrative Assistant V 41 11Private Secretary I 41 11\n8Administrative Assistant V 42 11Private Secretary I 42 11\n9Administrative Assistant V 43 11Private Secretary I 43 11\n10Administrative Assistant V 44 11Private Secretary I 44 11\n11Administrative Assistant V 60 11Private Secretary I 60 11\n12Administrative Assistant V 61 11Private Secretary I 61 11\n13Administrative Assistant V 62 11Private Secretary I 62 11\nSection 4. Repealing Clause – All ordinances or resolutions or laws of local \napplication and effect inconsistent hereto are hereby modified, superseded, and \nrepealed accordingly.\nSection 5. Separability Clause - If, for any reason or reasons, any part or \nprovision hereto shall be held to be unconstitutional or invalid, other parts or provisions \nhereof which is not affected thereof shall continue to be in full force and effect.\nSection 6. Effectivity– This ordinance shall take effect immediately upon \napproval.\n\nCERTIFIED CORRECT (on records):\n                    \n      \n                      \n                                                ENACTED ON _________________________\nATTESTATION/CERTIFICATION\nI HEREBY ATTEST and CERTIFY that I presided over the 1\nst\n REGULAR \nSESSION of the 8\nth\n Sangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga \nSibugay and that the foregoing legislative measure has been approved and \nenacted during the aforesaid session.\nHON. REY ANDRE C. OLEGARIO \nPresiding Officer\nProvincial Vice-Governor \nAPPROVED by HER HONOR on _________________________ at the Province of \nZamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\n                                HON. ANN K. HOFER\n                          Provincial Governor', '2025-12-03 15:19:10', '2025-12-03 15:19:10'),
(2, 2, 1, NULL, '2022,subsidy-to-all-barangays,hon-chennie-s-delos-reyes.pdf', 'ordinances/provincial/2022,subsidy-to-all-barangays,hon-chennie-s-delos-reyes.pdf', 1014866, 'application/pdf', 'First District\r\n       HON. MARIE YVONNE V. PALMA\r\n                        Assistant Floor Leader \r\n         Chairman: Senior Citizen, Differently Abled Persons,\r\n         Women, Children, Family & Other Social Services,\r\n         Education, Science, Arts & Culture\r\n       HON. ALLAN B. ESCAMILLAN \r\n          Chairman: Food & Agriculture, Energy, \r\n          Electrification, Public Utilities & Transportation\r\n       HON. JESSIE R. LAGAS \r\n          Chairman: Land Use, Housing, Rural & Urban \r\n          Development, Ethics & Good Government, and\r\n          Environment, Forest, Rivers & Inland Waters\r\n       HON. PEPITO S. YANGA, JR. \r\n       Chairman: Human Rights, Labor, Justice and\r\n          Employment, and Privileges, \r\n       ATTY. MARLO C. BANCORO \r\n          Chairman: Finance, Revenue, Way & Means, \r\n          Rules, Ordinances & Resolutions, Infrastructure,\r\n          Public   Works, & Engineering, Asset & Manage-\r\n          ment, Franchises, Games, & Amusements,\r\n          Municipal Affairs, & Legislative Oversight\r\n                Second District\r\n       HON. RICHARD D. OLEGARIO\r\n                              Floor Leader\r\n         Chairman:   Appropriations, Cooperatives Deve-\r\n         lopment, NGOs, PO’s, People Empowerment, \r\n         Gender & Development  & Steering Committee & \r\n         Inter-Agency Affairs, \r\nHON. MA. BELLA C. JAVIER \r\n        Chairman : Health, Information Communication\r\n        Technology (ICT), Rural Impact Sourcing (RIS) &\r\n        Computerization, International Relations & External\r\n        Affairs, & Economic Enterprise and Privatization\r\nHON. GERALD M. ACOSTA \r\n                   Assistant Floor Leader\r\n Chairman : Mining and Other Resources, & Fishery\r\n        and Coastal Resources. \r\nHON. CHENNIE S. DELOS REYES \r\n        Chairman : Peace  &  Order, Calamities, Fire & \r\n        Public Safety\r\n      HON. MARIA ESPERANZA CORAZON D.\r\nRILLERA-HADJIULA\r\n       Chairman: Tourism, & Appointments and Other\r\n       Personnel Concerns\r\nSectoral Representatives \r\n       HON. JERRY R. LAGAS \r\n          President : Liga ng mga Barangay\r\n          Chairman: Barangay Affairs, Trade , Industry & \r\n          Special Investments\r\n  \r\n      HON. MUJAHID C. JAJURIE \r\n         President : Provincial Councilor’s League\r\n        Chairman: Legislative Tracking & Analysis\r\n      HON. NATH ANTHONY R. EUDELA\r\n        President : Sangguniang Kabataan, \r\n        Chairman: Youth & Sports Development\r\n  \r\n  \r\n  \r\n \r\n  \r\n  \r\n \r\n  \r\nRepublic of the Philippines\r\nPROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY\r\n                                    Municipality of Ipil\r\nEXCERPT from the minutes of the 10\r\nth\r\n Regular Session of the 8\r\nth \r\nSangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga \r\nSibugay held at the Legislative Building, Capitol Hills, Ipil Heights, \r\nIpil, Zamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\r\n  \r\nAuthor: HON. CHENNIE S. DELOS REYES\r\n(Board Member, 2\r\nND\r\n District)\r\n                                        Co-Authors : HON. RICHARD DY OLEGARIO\r\n                                                          (Board Member, 2\r\nND\r\n District)\r\n                                                            ATTY. MARLO C. BANCORO \r\n                                                               (Board Member, 1\r\nST\r\n District)\r\nAN ORDINANCE PROVIDING FINANCIAL \r\nSUBSIDY TO ALL BARANGAYS IN THE PROVINCE \r\nOF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY AS ADDITIONAL \r\nFUNDING SUPPORT FOR CULTURAL AND SPORTS \r\nACTIVITIES DURING COMMEMORATION OF \r\nTHEIR ARAW NG BARANGAY.\r\nBE ENACTED, by the 8\r\nTH\r\n SANGGUNIANG PANLALAWIGAN \r\nof the PROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY , \r\nin session duly assembled, and\r\nORDAINED THAT:\r\nSection 1. Title – This ordinance shall be known and \r\nthereafter referred to as AN ORDINANCE PROVIDING \r\nFINANCIAL SUBSIDY TO ALL BARANGAYS IN THE \r\nPROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY AS ADDITIONAL \r\nFUNDING SUPPORT FOR CULTURAL AND SPORTS \r\nACTIVITIES DURING COMMEMORATION OF THEIR \r\nARAW NG BARANGAY.\r\nSection 2. Financial Subsidy during Araw ng \r\nBarangay. An amount of at least Twenty Thousand Pesos \r\n(Php20,000.00) shall be appropriated annually as financial \r\nsubsidy to every barangay in celebration of their Araw ng \r\nBarangay. The said amount shall be utilized as augmentation \r\nfund to defray their various expenses on cultural and sports \r\nactivities during the celebration. The said amount shall be \r\ndownloaded to the account of the barangay and shall be \r\nsubject to the COA rules and regulations on expenditures and \r\nliquidations.\r\nSection 3. Source of Fund. The amount of Twenty \r\nThousand Pesos (Php20,000.00) per barangay shall be \r\nappropriated annually from the general fund of the province of \r\nZamboanga Sibugay under the account code of subsidy to the \r\nbarangay or cultural and sports activities.\r\n\r\nSection 4. Repealing Clause - All ordinances, resolutions or laws of \r\nlocal application and effect inconsistent hereto are hereby modified, \r\nsuperseded, and repealed accordingly.\r\nSection 5. Separability Clause – If for any reason or reasons, any part \r\nor provisions of this ordinance shall be held to be unconstitutional or invalid, other \r\nparts or provisions hereof which are not affected thereby shall continue to be in \r\nfull force and effect.\r\nSection 6. Effectivity -This ordinance shall take effect immediately \r\nupon approval.\r\nCERTIFIED CORRECT (on records):\r\n                    \r\n      \r\n                      \r\n                                                ENACTED ON _________________________\r\nATTESTATION/CERTIFICATION\r\nI HEREBY ATTEST and CERTIFY that I presided over the 10\r\nTH\r\n REGULAR \r\nSESSION of the 8\r\nth\r\n Sangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga \r\nSibugay and that the foregoing legislative measure has been approved and \r\nenacted during the aforesaid session.\r\nHON. REY ANDRE C. OLEGARIO \r\nPresiding Officer\r\nProvincial Vice-Governor \r\nAPPROVED by HER HONOR on _________________________ at the Province \r\nof Zamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\r\n                                HON. DULCE ANN K. HOFER\r\n                          Provincial Governor', '2025-12-03 15:36:45', '2025-12-03 15:36:45'),
(3, 3, 1, NULL, '2022,naming-the-new-provincial,atty-marlo-c-bancoro.pdf', 'ordinances/provincial/2022,naming-the-new-provincial,atty-marlo-c-bancoro.pdf', 1005440, 'application/pdf', 'First District\r\n       HON. MARIE YVONNE V. PALMA\r\n                        Assistant Floor Leader \r\n         Chairman: Senior Citizen, Differently Abled Persons,\r\n         Women, Children, Family & Other Social Services,\r\n         Education, Science, Arts & Culture\r\n       HON. ALLAN B. ESCAMILLAN \r\n          Chairman: Food & Agriculture, Energy, \r\n          Electrification, Public Utilities & Transportation\r\n       HON. JESSIE R. LAGAS \r\n          Chairman: Land Use, Housing, Rural & Urban \r\n          Development, Ethics & Good Government, and\r\n          Environment, Forest, Rivers & Inland Waters\r\n       HON. PEPITO S. YANGA, JR. \r\n       Chairman: Human Rights, Labor, Justice and\r\n          Employment, and Privileges, \r\n       ATTY. MARLO C. BANCORO \r\n          Chairman: Finance, Revenue, Way & Means, \r\n          Rules, Ordinances & Resolutions, Infrastructure,\r\n          Public   Works, & Engineering, Asset & Manage-\r\n          ment, Franchises, Games, & Amusements,\r\n          Municipal Affairs, & Legislative Oversight\r\n                Second District\r\n       HON. RICHARD D. OLEGARIO\r\n                              Floor Leader\r\n         Chairman:   Appropriations, Cooperatives Deve-\r\n         lopment, NGOs, PO’s, People Empowerment, \r\n         Gender & Development  & Steering Committee & \r\n         Inter-Agency Affairs, \r\nHON. MA. BELLA C. JAVIER \r\n        Chairman : Health, Information Communication\r\n        Technology (ICT), Rural Impact Sourcing (RIS) &\r\n        Computerization, International Relations & External\r\n        Affairs, & Economic Enterprise and Privatization\r\nHON. GERALD M. ACOSTA \r\n                   Assistant Floor Leader\r\n Chairman : Mining and Other Resources, & Fishery\r\n        and Coastal Resources. \r\nHON. CHENNIE S. DELOS REYES \r\n        Chairman : Peace  &  Order, Calamities, Fire & \r\n        Public Safety\r\n      HON. MARIA ESPERANZA CORAZON D.\r\nRILLERA-HADJIULA\r\n       Chairman: Tourism, & Appointments and Other\r\n       Personnel Concerns\r\nSectoral Representatives \r\n       HON. JERRY R. LAGAS \r\n          President : Liga ng mga Barangay\r\n          Chairman: Barangay Affairs, Trade , Industry & \r\n          Special Investments\r\n  \r\n      HON. MUJAHID C. JAJURIE \r\n         President : Provincial Councilor’s League\r\n        Chairman: Legislative Tracking & Analysis\r\n      HON. NATH ANTHONY R. EUDELA\r\n        President : Sangguniang Kabataan, \r\n        Chairman: Youth & Sports Development\r\n  \r\n  \r\n  \r\n \r\n  \r\n  \r\n \r\n  \r\nRepublic of the Philippines\r\nPROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY\r\n                                    Municipality of Ipil\r\nEXCERPT from the minutes of the 11\r\nth\r\n Regular Session of the 8\r\nth \r\nSangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga \r\nSibugay held at the Legislative Building, Capitol Hills, Ipil Heights, \r\nIpil, Zamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\r\n  \r\nAuthors: \r\nATTY. MARLO C. BANCORO\r\n(Board Member, 1\r\nST\r\n District)\r\nHON. DARA MAY L. CATALUÑA\r\n(Board Member, Ex-Officio)\r\nAN ORDINANCE NAMING THE NEW PROVINCIAL HOS-\r\nPITAL LOCATED AT BARANGAY TENAN, IPIL, ZAM-\r\nBOANGA SIBUGAY AS THE DR. GEORGE TOCAO HOFER \r\nMEDICAL CENTER PURSUANT TO SECTION 13, CHAPTER \r\n2, TITLE I, BOOK 1 OF REPUBLIC ACT NO. 7160, OTHER-\r\nWISE KNOWN AS THE LOCAL GOVERNMENT CODE OF \r\n1991. \r\nBE ENACTED, by the 8\r\nTH\r\n SANGGUNIANG PANLALAWIGAN \r\nof the PROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY , \r\nin session duly assembled, and\r\nORDAINED THAT:\r\nSection 1. Title – This ordinance shall be known and thereafter \r\nreferred to as “AN ORDINANCE NAMING THE NEW \r\nPROVINCIAL HOSPITAL LOCATED AT BARANGAY \r\nTENAN, IPIL, ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY AS THE \r\n“DR. GEORGE TOCAO HOFER MEDICAL CENTER”.\r\nSection 2.  Rationale and Legal Authority 	.  The naming of the \r\nprovincial hospital alluded to is to confer permanent \r\nidentity to the same and to avoid confusion to the \r\npublic notably because of the numerous government \r\nhospitals in place. The naming is pursuant to Section \r\n13, Chapter 2, Title 1, Book 1 of Republic Act No. 7160, \r\notherwise known as the Local Government Code of \r\n1991.   \r\nSection 3. THE DR. GEORGE TOCAO HOFER MEDICAL CEN-\r\nTER.- The newly constructed provincial hospital located \r\nat Barangay Tenan, Ipil, Zamboanga Sibugay is hereby \r\nnamed and declared as the “DR. GEORGE TOCAO \r\nHOFER MEDICAL CENTER” in the Province of \r\nZamboanga Sibugay, for all legal intents and purposes.\r\nSection 4.  Separability Clause. If any provision of this Ordinance \r\nis declared invalid and unconstitutional, other \r\nprovisions not affected thereby shall remain valid and \r\nsubsisting.\r\n\r\nSection 5. Repealing Clause. All orders or parts thereof, and ordinances, re-\r\nsolutions or laws of local application and effect inconsistent hereto are \r\nhereby modified, superseded, and repealed accordingly. \r\nSection 6. Effectivity - This Ordinance shall take effect fifteen (15) days \r\nfrom publication hereof.\r\n CERTIFIED CORRECT (on records): \r\n                    \r\n       NICASIO M. PEÑA, LLB, CSPE \r\n                           Secretary \r\n                           \r\n                                                       ENACTED ON ________________________\r\nATTESTATION/CERTIFICATION\r\nI HEREBY ATTEST and CERTIFY that I presided over the 11\r\nTH\r\n REGULAR SESSION of \r\nthe 8\r\nth\r\n Sangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga Sibugay and that the \r\nforegoing legislative measure has been enacted and approved during the aforesaid \r\nsession.\r\nHON. REY ANDRE C. OLEGARIO \r\nPresiding Officer\r\nProvincial Vice-Governor \r\nAPPROVED by HER HONOR on _________________________ in the Province \r\nof Zamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\r\n                                HON. DULCE ANN K. HOFER\r\n                          Provincial Governor', '2025-12-03 15:39:31', '2025-12-03 15:39:31'),
(4, 4, 1, NULL, '2022,barge-fare-rate,atty-marlo-c-bancoro.pdf', 'ordinances/provincial/2022,barge-fare-rate,atty-marlo-c-bancoro.pdf', 1551304, 'application/pdf', 'First District\r\n       HON. MARIE YVONNE V. PALMA\r\n                        Assistant Floor Leader \r\n         Chairman: Senior Citizen, Differently Abled Persons,\r\n         Women, Children, Family & Other Social Services,\r\n         Education, Science, Arts & Culture\r\n       HON. ALLAN B. ESCAMILLAN \r\n          Chairman: Food & Agriculture, Energy, \r\n          Electrification, Public Utilities & Transportation\r\n       HON. JESSIE R. LAGAS \r\n          Chairman: Land Use, Housing, Rural & Urban \r\n          Development, Ethics & Good Government, and\r\n          Environment, Forest, Rivers & Inland Waters\r\n       HON. PEPITO S. YANGA, JR. \r\n       Chairman: Human Rights, Labor, Justice and\r\n          Employment, and Privileges, \r\n       ATTY. MARLO C. BANCORO \r\n          Chairman: Finance, Revenue, Way & Means, \r\n          Rules, Ordinances & Resolutions, Infrastructure,\r\n          Public   Works, & Engineering, Asset & Manage-\r\n          ment, Franchises, Games, & Amusements,\r\n          Municipal Affairs, & Legislative Oversight\r\n                Second District\r\n       HON. RICHARD D. OLEGARIO\r\n                              Floor Leader\r\n         Chairman:   Appropriations, Cooperatives Deve-\r\n         lopment, NGOs, PO’s, People Empowerment, \r\n         Gender & Development  & Steering Committee & \r\n         Inter-Agency Affairs, \r\nHON. MA. BELLA C. JAVIER \r\n        Chairman : Health, Information Communication\r\n        Technology (ICT), Rural Impact Sourcing (RIS) &\r\n        Computerization, International Relations & External\r\n        Affairs, & Economic Enterprise and Privatization\r\nHON. GERALD M. ACOSTA \r\n                   Assistant Floor Leader\r\n Chairman : Mining and Other Resources, & Fishery\r\n        and Coastal Resources. \r\nHON. CHENNIE S. DELOS REYES \r\n        Chairman : Peace  &  Order, Calamities, Fire & \r\n        Public Safety\r\n      HON. MARIA ESPERANZA CORAZON D.\r\nRILLERA-HADJIULA\r\n       Chairman: Tourism, & Appointments and Other\r\n       Personnel Concerns\r\nSectoral Representatives \r\n       HON. JERRY R. LAGAS \r\n          President : Liga ng mga Barangay\r\n          Chairman: Barangay Affairs, Trade , Industry & \r\n          Special Investments\r\n  \r\n      HON. MUJAHID C. JAJURIE \r\n         President : Provincial Councilor’s League\r\n        Chairman: Legislative Tracking & Analysis\r\n      HON. NATH ANTHONY R. EUDELA\r\n        President : Sangguniang Kabataan, \r\n        Chairman: Youth & Sports Development\r\n  \r\n  \r\n  \r\n \r\n  \r\n  \r\n \r\n  \r\nRepublic of the Philippines\r\nPROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY\r\n                                    Municipality of Ipil\r\nEXCERPT from the minutes of the 11\r\nth\r\n Regular Session of the 8\r\nth \r\nSangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga \r\nSibugay held at the Legislative Building, Capitol Hills, Ipil Heights, \r\nIpil, Zamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\r\n  \r\n    Author: ATTY. MARLO C. BANCORO \r\n      (Board Member, 1\r\nST\r\n District)\r\nAN ORDINANCE AMENDING SECTION 2 OF ORDINANCE \r\nNO. 2015-442 PROVIDING FARE RATE OF FERRY \r\nSERVICES (PROVINCIAL BARGE) OPERATING IN \r\nGUICAM AND HULA-HULA AND VICE VERSA, IN THE \r\nMUNICIPALITIES OF MABUHAY AND ALICIA, \r\nZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY.\r\nBE ENACTED, by the 8\r\nTH\r\n SANGGUNIANG PANLALAWIGAN \r\nof the PROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY , \r\nin session duly assembled, and\r\nORDAINED THAT:\r\nSection 1. Title – This ordinance shall be known and \r\nthereafter referred to as “AN ORDINANCE AMENDING \r\nSECTION 2 OF ORDINANCE NO. 2015-442 PROVIDING \r\nFARE RATE OF FERRY SERVICES (PROVINCIAL BARGE) \r\nOPERATING IN GUICAM AND HULA-HULA AND VICE \r\nVERSA, IN THE MUNICIPALITIES OF MABUHAY AND \r\nALICIA, ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY.\r\nSection 2. Fare Rate- There shall be provided and \r\nimposed fare rate per ferry (one way service) in the operation of \r\nprovincial ferry services in the municipalities of Mabuhay and \r\nAlicia in the Province of Zamboanga Sibugay as follows: \r\nHEAVY EQUIPMENT\r\na. Bulldozer	P 2,000,00/unit\r\nb. Grader   1,500.00/unit\r\nc. Compactor   1,500.00/unit\r\nd. Backhoe   1,500.00/unit\r\ne. Payloader   1,500.00/unit\r\nHEAVY EQUIPMENT\r\na. With cargo	P 1,500.00/unit\r\nb. Without cargo   1,000.00/unit\r\nCARGO TRUCKS ( BELOW 6 TONS)\r\na. With cargo	P   650.00/unit\r\nb. Without cargo     500.00/unit\r\nc. Bongo truck with cargo     450.00/unit\r\nd. Bongo truck without cargo     350.00/unit\r\n\r\nMulti-cab with cargo    275.00/unit\r\nMulti-cab without cargo    250.00/unit\r\nCARGO TRUCKS ( ABOVE  6 TONS)\r\na. With cargo	P   900.00/unit\r\nb. Without cargo     750.00/unit\r\nPUBLIC UTILITY VEHICLES\r\na. Bus excluding passengers	P  400.00/unit\r\nb. Jeepney excluding passengers     250.00/unit\r\nc. Tricycle with cargo     150.00/unit\r\nd. Tricycle without cargo     100.00/unit\r\nPUBLIC UTILITY AND OTHER CAR/ VEHICLES\r\na. Owner type	P 250.00/unit\r\nb. Bicycle      20.00/unit\r\nc. Funeral car   130.00/unit\r\nd. Others   130.00/unit\r\nANIMALS/ LIVESTOCKS\r\na. Carabao	P 150.00\r\nb. Horse   150.00\r\nc. Cow   150.00\r\nd. Pig     25.00 \r\ne. Goat     20.00 \r\nf. Others     20.00\r\nAGRICULTURAL PRODUCTS\r\na. Tobacco/pasta(Below 20 kgs) P   30.00\r\nb. Tobacco/pasta(Below 20 kgs                   \r\n         	but not exceeding 40 kgs )    40.00\r\nc. Rice/50 kgs     10.00\r\nd. Corn/50 kgs      10.00\r\ne. Fruits (below 20 kgs )     10.00\r\nf. Fruits (above 20 kgs )     10.00\r\nCONSTRUCTION MATERIALS\r\nG.I. PIPES\r\na. ½ “     Diameter x 20	P     5.00/unit\r\nb. ¼ “     Diameter x 20       5.00/unit\r\nc. 1 “     Diameter x 20       5.00/unit\r\nd. 1 1/16“  Diameter x 20       5.00/unit\r\ne. 1 ½ “     Diameter x 20       5.00/unit\r\nf. 2“    Diameter x 20     10.00/unit\r\ng. 3“    Diameter x 20     10.00/unit\r\nh. 4“    Diameter x 20     10.00/unit\r\n\r\nPVC/UPVC\r\na. 1 ½ “    Diameter x 20 P    5.00/unit\r\nb. 2 “   Diameter x 20       5.00/unit\r\nc. 2 ½ “    Diameter x 20     10.00/unit\r\nd. 3“   Diameter x 20     10.00/unit\r\ne. 6“   Diameter x 20     10.00/unit\r\nf.  8“   Diameter x 20     10.00/unit\r\nP.E. PIPES\r\na. 1 ½ “    Diameter x 20	P   15.00/unit \r\nb. ¾ ‘   Diameter x 20      15.00/unit\r\nc. 1“   Diameter x 20      15.00/unit\r\nd. 1 1/16“ Diameter x 20      20.00/unit\r\ne. 1 ½ “    Diameter x 20      20.00/unit\r\nf. 2”   Diameter x 20      20.00/unit\r\ng. 2 ½ “   Diameter x 20      20.00/unit\r\nh. Cement      10.00/bag\r\ni. Steel Bar (5mm-20’)       10.00/unit\r\nj. Plywood   ¼ x 4”x 8’ & ½ 4”x8’                   5.00/sheet\r\nk. Plywood ¾ x 4”x 8’ & 1x 4”x8’      10.00/sheet\r\nl. G.I corrugated sheet ( gauge 31, gauge18x3 x8)           5.00/sheet\r\nm. G.I plain sheet        5.00/sheet\r\nn. Cyclone barbed wire      15.00/roll\r\no. Tiles        5.00/box\r\nAQUA MARINE  PRODUCT\r\na. Crabs per box 	P    20.00\r\nb. Fish/ shrimps (Below 20 kgs)      20.00\r\nc. Fish/ shrimps (Below 20 kgs \r\n    but not exceeding 50 kgs)         20.00\r\nd. Shells(Below 20 kgs)      10.00\r\ne. Shells(Below 20 kgs  but not exceeding 40 kgs )     15.00\r\n f. Seaweeds (Fresh) per pack      10.00\r\ng. Seaweeds (dried)       12.00\r\nh. Dried fish per pack        10.00\r\nAPPLIANCES\r\na. Refrigerator	P   30.00/unit\r\nb. Television     40.00/unit\r\nc. Karaoke/Videoke     20.00/unit\r\nd. Air conditioning unit     20.00/unit\r\ne. Other of similar nature     20.00/unit\r\nFURNITURE AND FIXTURES\r\na. Sala set (made of bamboo)	P   75.00/set\r\nb. Sala set (made of wood/steel)     75.00/set\r\nc. Other of similar nature (sala set)     75.00/set\r\n d. Computers for business purposes     20.00/unit\r\ne. Other modern technology devices\r\n    for business purposes     20.00/unit\r\n\r\nUKAY- UKAY\r\n(Relief clothes sold in the market, usually no arranged or placed in\r\nhangers instead they are simply dumped in mountains of clothes and\r\nthe consumers  would dig and turn them over to find the desired \r\ngarments or buying and selling used clothes;\r\na.  Below 20 kilos      25.00\r\nb.  Above 20 kilos      30.00\r\nLIQUIFIED PETROLEUM/ GASOLINE/ OIL AND LUBRICANTS\r\na. Gasoline/ Petroleum gas/ Oil/ and LubricantsP     5.00\r\nb. Tank with content per tank     15.00\r\nc. LPG Tank without content per tank     10.00\r\nPASSENGERS 	FREE\r\na. Passengers regardless of residence shall be exempted from \r\npayment of imposable fare.\r\nb. All registered government vehicles and all vehicles of elected \r\nprovincial officials of Zamboanga Sibugay and elected municipal \r\nand barangay officials from the municipalities of Mabuhay, Talusan \r\nand Olutanga, Zamboanga Sibugay are exempted from payment of \r\nimposable fare.\r\nSPECIAL TRIP\r\na. Private utility vehicle (owner type) P  1,500.00\r\nb. Fish car    1,500.00\r\nc. Cargo truck with cargo    1,500.00\r\nd. Cargo truck without cargo    1,000.00\r\ne. Ten wheeler truck and other heavy equipment     1,500.00\r\nOTHERS\r\na. Personal baggage above 15 kgs P      10.00\r\nSection 3. Separability Clause - If, for any reason or reasons, any part or \r\nprovision hereto shall be held to be unconstitutional or invalid, other parts or \r\nprovisions hereof which is not affected thereof shall continue to be in full force and \r\neffect.\r\nSection 4. Repealing Clause – All ordinances or resolutions or laws of \r\nlocal application and effect inconsistent hereto are hereby modified, superseded, \r\nand repealed accordingly.\r\nSection 5. Effectivity Clause – This ordinance shall take effect \r\nimmediately upon approval.\r\n\r\nCERTIFIED CORRECT (on records):\r\n                    \r\n      \r\n                      \r\n                                                ENACTED ON _________________________\r\nATTESTATION/CERTIFICATION\r\nI HEREBY ATTEST and CERTIFY that I presided over the 11\r\nTH\r\n REGULAR \r\nSESSION of the 8\r\nth\r\n Sangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga \r\nSibugay and that the foregoing legislative measure has been approved and \r\nenacted during the aforesaid session.\r\nHON. REY ANDRE C. OLEGARIO \r\nPresiding Officer\r\nProvincial Vice-Governor \r\nAPPROVED by HER HONOR on _________________________ at the Province of \r\nZamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\r\n                                HON. DULCE ANN K. HOFER\r\n                          Provincial Governor', '2025-12-03 15:43:24', '2025-12-03 15:43:24'),
(5, 5, 1, NULL, '2022,create-their-own-internet,hon-ma-bella-chiong--javier.pdf', 'ordinances/provincial/2022,create-their-own-internet,hon-ma-bella-chiong--javier.pdf', 1147988, 'application/pdf', 'First District\r\n       HON. MARIE YVONNE V. PALMA\r\n                        Assistant Floor Leader \r\n         Chairman: Senior Citizen, Differently Abled Persons,\r\n         Women, Children, Family & Other Social Services,\r\n         Education, Science, Arts & Culture\r\n       HON. ALLAN B. ESCAMILLAN \r\n          Chairman: Food & Agriculture, Energy, \r\n          Electrification, Public Utilities & Transportation\r\n       HON. JESSIE R. LAGAS \r\n          Chairman: Land Use, Housing, Rural & Urban \r\n          Development, Ethics & Good Government, and\r\n          Environment, Forest, Rivers & Inland Waters\r\n       HON. PEPITO S. YANGA, JR. \r\n       Chairman: Human Rights, Labor, Justice and\r\n          Employment, and Privileges, \r\n       ATTY. MARLO C. BANCORO \r\n          Chairman: Finance, Revenue, Way & Means, \r\n          Rules, Ordinances & Resolutions, Infrastructure,\r\n          Public   Works, & Engineering, Asset & Manage-\r\n          ment, Franchises, Games, & Amusements,\r\n          Municipal Affairs, & Legislative Oversight\r\n                Second District\r\n       HON. RICHARD D. OLEGARIO\r\n                              Floor Leader\r\n         Chairman:   Appropriations, Cooperatives Deve-\r\n         lopment, NGOs, PO’s, People Empowerment, \r\n         Gender & Development  & Steering Committee & \r\n         Inter-Agency Affairs, \r\nHON. MA. BELLA C. JAVIER \r\n        Chairman : Health, Information Communication\r\n        Technology (ICT), Rural Impact Sourcing (RIS) &\r\n        Computerization, International Relations & External\r\n        Affairs, & Economic Enterprise and Privatization\r\nHON. GERALD M. ACOSTA \r\n                   Assistant Floor Leader\r\n Chairman : Mining and Other Resources, & Fishery\r\n        and Coastal Resources. \r\nHON. CHENNIE S. DELOS REYES \r\n        Chairman : Peace  &  Order, Calamities, Fire & \r\n        Public Safety\r\n      HON. MARIA ESPERANZA CORAZON D.\r\nRILLERA-HADJIULA\r\n       Chairman: Tourism, & Appointments and Other\r\n       Personnel Concerns\r\nSectoral Representatives \r\n       HON. JERRY R. LAGAS \r\n          President : Liga ng mga Barangay\r\n          Chairman: Barangay Affairs, Trade , Industry & \r\n          Special Investments\r\n  \r\n      HON. MUJAHID C. JAJURIE \r\n         President : Provincial Councilor’s League\r\n        Chairman: Legislative Tracking & Analysis\r\n      HON. NATH ANTHONY R. EUDELA\r\n        President : Sangguniang Kabataan, \r\n        Chairman: Youth & Sports Development\r\n  \r\n  \r\n  \r\n \r\n  \r\n  \r\n \r\n  \r\nRepublic of the Philippines\r\nPROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY\r\n                                    Municipality of Ipil\r\nEXCERPT from the minutes of the 13\r\nth\r\n Regular Session of the 8\r\nth \r\nSangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga \r\nSibugay held at the Legislative Building, Capitol Hills, Ipil Heights, \r\nIpil, Zamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\r\n  \r\nAuthor:\r\nHON. MA. BELLA CHIONG -JAVIER\r\nBoard Member, 2\r\nND\r\n District\r\nHON. PEPITO S. YANGA, JR. \r\nBoard Member, 1\r\nst\r\n District \r\n  \r\nHON. MARIE YVONNE V. PALMA \r\nBoard Member, 1\r\nst\r\n District) \r\n(Co-authors)\r\nAN ORDINANCE REQUIRING ALL LOCAL GOVERNMENT \r\nUNITS (LGU) IN THE SIXTEEN (16) MUNICIPALITIES OF \r\nTHE PROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY TO CREATE \r\nTHEIR OWN INTERNET WEBSITE AND PROVIDING \r\nFUNDS FOR THE PURPOSE.\r\nBE ENACTED, by the 8\r\nTH\r\n SANGGUNIANG PANLALAWIGAN \r\nof the PROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA SIBUGAY , \r\nin session duly assembled, and\r\nORDAINED THAT:\r\nSection 1. Title – This ordinance shall be known and \r\nthereafter referred to as “AN ORDINANCE REQUIRING ALL \r\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT UNITS (LGU) IN THE SIXTEEN (16) \r\nMUNICIPALITIES OF THE PROVINCE OF ZAMBOANGA \r\nSIBUGAY TO CREATE THEIR OWN INTERNET WEBSITE \r\nAND PROVIDING FUNDS FOR THE PURPOSE ”.\r\nSection 2. Purposes and Benefits – The purposes and \r\nbenefits in creating LGU’s own website are as follows:\r\na.Ensure and ease in making business;\r\nb.Uplift the economy of the locality and the province \r\nthrough easily accessible communication, information, \r\nmarketing and advertisement of their locality;\r\nc.Online presence for 24/7 and provide easy access on \r\njob opportunities;\r\nd.Create brand awareness and provide easy access to \r\nshowcasing of locally products and services; and\r\ne.Provide wider demographic reach.\r\n\r\nSection 3. Funding Allocation – There shall be allocated funds for the \r\noperation and activities for website development and other ICT programs, \r\nsubject to availability of provincial funds.  \r\nSection 4. Repealing Clause. All local ordinances and enactments, \r\nexecutive orders, resolutions, memoranda, circulars or any part thereof \r\ncontrary to or inconsistent with the provisions of this Ordinance is hereby \r\nrepealed, modified or amended accordingly.\r\nSection 5. Separability Clause. If, for any reason or reasons, any part \r\nor provision of this Ordinance shall be held to be unconstitutional or invalid, \r\nother parts or provisions hereof which are not affected thereby shall stand and \r\ncontinue to be in full force and effect.\r\nSection 6. Effectivity. This ordinance shall take effect immediately upon \r\napproval.\r\nCERTIFIED CORRECT (on records):\r\n                    \r\n      \r\n                      \r\n                                                ENACTED ON _________________________\r\nATTESTATION/CERTIFICATION\r\nI HEREBY ATTEST and CERTIFY that I presided over the 13\r\nth\r\n REGULAR \r\nSESSION of the 8\r\nth\r\n Sangguniang Panlalawigan of the Province of Zamboanga \r\nSibugay and that the foregoing legislative measure has been approved and \r\nenacted during the aforesaid session.\r\nHON. REY ANDRE C. OLEGARIO \r\nPresiding Officer\r\nProvincial Vice-Governor\r\n\r\nAPPROVED by HER HONOR on _________________________ at the Province \r\nof Zamboanga Sibugay, Philippines.\r\n                                HON. DULCE ANN K. HOFER\r\n                          Provincial Governor', '2025-12-03 15:59:41', '2025-12-03 15:59:41'),
